    "descriptions": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_447ad8d73a70",
            "level": {
              "value": 2
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "You make yourself into a living mirror, becoming a double of someone unremarkable, and you slip into exactly the role that can get you past security or into a sensitive facility. You become an expert in Deception. You gain the Assume a Role activity.\n\n**Assume a Role**\nYou quickly and accurately learn how to do mundane jobs or at least copy the movements enough to appear as if you do. A chosen role can take many forms\u2014from cook, cleaner, or librarian to cult member, priest, or duke\u2014but it's always a role and never a specific individual.\nYou perform the Impersonate activity to pass as a member of the role you observed and gain a +1 circumstance bonus to any Deception checks you attempt in your impersonation. This takes the normal amount of time it takes you to Impersonate. You also choose one Lore skill relevant to that role (such as Farming Lore for a farmer). While in your role, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to checks for that Lore skill, and if you're untrained in it, you can use your level as your proficiency bonus.\nYou stop assuming the role after 24 hours, if you start studying for a new role, or if you choose to."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
